@startuml
!include https://raw.githubusercontent.com/proveo-ca/identity/main/proveo.puml
title Toolchain e2e — proving toolchain provisioning is true as BEHAVIOUR

' covers: e2e/toolchain_test.go, internal/contract/toolchain_test.go,
' covers: e2e/testdata/polyglot22
'
' REMOVED 2026-10-30 with the LSP feature (_spec/defs/harness-image-layers.puml):
' the language matrix, the fixture-coverage check, the LSP opt-outs
' (PROVEO_LSP_INSTALL, PROVEO_LSP_MIN_FILES), TestToolchainOptOutStillSeesInstalledServers
' and the contract half's registry checks. polyglot22 stays as a polyglot
' workspace for idempotence and the auto-install opt-out.
'   the pane-echo rules these probes obey . _spec/tests/testing-strategy.puml
'   what the seed actually installs ....... _spec/_runtimes/toolchain-provisioning.puml
'
' ── WHAT "WARM" MEANS, AND WHY THE STORE IS THE THING MEASURED ─────────────
' Migrated from e2e/toolchain_test.go 2026-09-16; these are the properties the
' suite depends on rather than details of one helper.
'
' WARM IS TWO RUNS SHARING ONE PROVEO HOME, and that home is also the toolchain
' store — sbx tells the sandbox where it is through `PROVEO_STATE_HOME`. So the
' idempotence case is not "run it twice and see"; it is "write the store, then
' prove the next run reads it".
'
' THE HONEST MEASURE IS WHAT THE SEED INSTALLED, not what is present. By the time
' an operator has a prompt, provisioning is the seed's work — counting anything
' else credits the image, or the developer's own hand, with the restore.
'
' AND A FAILURE HAS TWO HALVES THAT LOOK IDENTICAL. The store is the HOST side of
' `proveo_sync_tools`, written at teardown and read by the next run's seed. A case
' that names the store's state when it fails separates "the save never wrote" from
' "the restore never read"; one that reports only "not installed" leaves both
' equally likely and neither testable.
'
' ── THE SEED RACE: A PROMPT IS NOT A FINISHED SANDBOX ──────────────────────
' sbx hands the operator a prompt WHILE the Kit's startup commands are still
' running, so a probe sent on sight of the prompt races the seed and loses to its
' install lock. Waiting on the prompt is the intuitive thing and it is wrong.
'
' The startup log is what closes it: it opens a line with "> " per command and
' closes each with "ok" or "fail", so the two counts meeting is the seed being
' finished with the sandbox. That is an observable end state rather than a sleep,
' which is the same rule the pane-echo section of testing-strategy.puml states for
' markers — never wait on a timer where the system publishes a completion.
'
' ── THE LIB IS DRIVEN WHERE IT RUNS ────────────────────────────────────────
' `runLib` exercises the entrypoint lib inside a sandbox the operator's own
' `proveo run` created, not a replica assembled by the test. The lib is baked at
' `/entrypoint-lib.sh` and the fixture is the sandbox's workspace, so the scripts'
' `/work` becomes `$PWD`. A replica would corroborate the replica.
'
' Its GitHub token requirement belongs inside the sandbox for the same reason: the
' mise installs would otherwise hit the 60/hr anonymous limit, and sbx injects the
' token for its own `github` service — so the host holding one proves nothing
' about what the installs can reach.

node "Layer 2 — contract (no Docker)" as L2 <<host>> {
  component "no image reinstalls its base's packages" as C3 <<app>>
}

node "Layer 4 — e2e (real images)" as L4 <<host>> {
  component "idempotence — warm PROVEO_HOME" as E2 <<app>>
  component "auto-install opt-out · fail-soft · no duplicates" as E3 <<app>>
  component "floor invariants — EVERY harness" as E4 <<app>>
  component "baked lib is CURRENT" as E5 <<app>>
}

database "testdata/polyglot22\none file per language" as FIX <<db>>
component "working-tree lib\nbind-mounted over the baked one" as LIVE <<app>>
component "stale image\nsource fixed, behaviour unchanged" as STALE <<error>>

FIX ARROW_MAIN E2
LIVE ARROW_MAIN E3 : no rebuild needed
E5 ARROW_ERROR STALE : the ONLY test that can see this

note right of L2
  **Source truth vs behavioural truth.** Layer 2
  proves the Dockerfiles agree as SOURCE on every
  ""go test ./..."". Layer 4 proves the seed's
  installs happen in a real image.
end note

note bottom of LIVE
  Mounting the working-tree lib over the baked one is what lets these run against
  uncommitted changes with no image rebuild — and is exactly why a stale image
  is invisible to them.
end note

note bottom of E5
  **The failure a source fix cannot cover.** The lib is COPIED into each image at
  build time, so a harness built before an edit keeps running the old helpers
  while the working tree looks correct. Every other test here mounts over that,
  so only a probe of the BAKED lib — no mount — can catch it. It names the
  rebuild command, because the fix is not live until the image is rebuilt.
end note

note bottom of E4
  One lib, three harnesses, three different floors: cursor carries no Node
  runtime. Testing only opencode left two images
  unverified — including whether ""plantuml"" reaches the runtime-free one,
  which was the whole point of moving it onto ""proveo/base"".
end note

note right of E2
  Opt-in behind PROVEO_TOOLCHAIN_TEST. It SKIPS
  rather than fails when no GitHub token is
  reachable: mise would hit the 60/hr anonymous
  limit, and the test would be flaky, not honest.
end note
@enduml
